    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <details><summary>What is the four-digit code in the Restaurant in Rooms &amp; Exits Chapter 2?</summary><p><b>6743</b>. It goes into the burgundy briefcase on the dining-room floor, the one with the cocktail-glass emblem on the front. The four golden drums read 6, 7, 4, 3 in our capture, and those are the four prices on the chalkboard menu behind the bar — 3.00, 6.00, 7.00 and 4.00 — taken in reading order.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What number goes into the plate-and-fork panel?</summary><p><b>18</b>. The teal panel has a plate, a plus sign and a fork above two digit boxes. Count the plates and forks set out on the dining tables: one setting gives 8 plates and 5 forks (13), a second gives 4 plates and 1 fork (5), and 13 plus 5 is 18. Both recordings we checked finish on 18.</p></details>
    <details><summary>What is the four-letter code in the Restaurant?</summary><p><b>FOOD</b>. The grey panel beside the service doorway holds four letter wheels. It already reads F-O-O-D when you first find it at 3:08, and the level ends once the wheels are back on that word after being scrambled.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I build the pizza?</summary><p>Open the bag, select <b>Dough</b>, press <b>Combine</b>, then tap <b>Tomato</b> — the slot becomes <b>Pizza</b>. Then select the Pizza and repeat Combine for each topping: Onion, Chili pepper and Cheese are the order our second recording follows, with Olives going in as well. Do not dismantle the half-built pizza; it reads as clutter and that is how people lose it.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How do I use the oven?</summary><p>Fit the <b>Oven button</b> first — the panel is inert without it. The left dial runs 0 to 7, the right dial is a timer at 15, 30, 45, 60 and 75, and there is a °C button plus a pink ON button. Set the timer to 75, choose a heat setting and press ON. We could not read the heat number twice, so this guide does not print one.</p></details>
    <details><summary>How long does the Restaurant take?</summary><p>Our capture finishes in <b>24:13</b> of level time, but the clip is sped up to roughly double speed, so it is eleven and a half minutes of footage. Nothing is timed and there is no fail state — the only thing that stretches the level is walking between the dining room and the kitchen without a list.</p></details>

